{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-09-29_11-09-41-hashicorp_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v1.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Apply creates a future on applyCh. The leader main loop assigns index/term and stores logs; only successful storage reports local match. Per-peer workers send real AppendEntries with previous-log identity, term and leader commit index. Receiver rejects stale terms or mismatched prefix, truncates conflicts, stores new suffix and updates configuration before successful response. Successful nonempty append or snapshot installation advances that worker's captured session commitment. Commitment counts only current voter IDs and requires a majority match reaching the first index of this tenure; leaderLoop consumes commitCh, records commitment and queues committed entries. Followers learn commit index from ordinary replication; empty independent heartbeat carries neither entries nor commit index. processLogs dispatches in order to runFSM; command completion follows Apply/ApplyBatch return, while the main-loop lastApplied value only tracks dispatch. Replication retry and snapshot fallback recover lagging peers.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-submit\",\n        \"B-dispatch\",\n        \"B-append\",\n        \"B-reply-match\",\n        \"B-commit\",\n        \"B-apply\",\n        \"B-recover\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-local-store\",\n        \"F-append-success\",\n        \"F-peer-match\",\n        \"F-commit\",\n        \"F-applied\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-api-apply\",\n        \"S-append\",\n        \"S-bootstrap\",\n        \"S-commitment\",\n        \"S-config-replay\",\n        \"S-dispatch-apply\",\n        \"S-follower\",\n        \"S-fsm-contract\",\n        \"S-fsm-worker\",\n        \"S-install\",\n        \"S-leader-loop\",\n        \"S-leader-session\",\n        \"S-net-fastpath\",\n        \"S-pipeline-consume\",\n        \"S-repl-membership\",\n        \"S-replicate\",\n        \"S-reply-match\",\n        \"S-send-snapshot\",\n        \"S-startup\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Startup reads durable term and log, restores snapshot/FSM and membership, replays suffix configurations and starts as Follower. Ordinary contact timeout campaigns only for a local voter. Optional pre-vote does not persist a vote; actual electSelf increments durable term, persists self-vote and sends one request per voter into a campaign-specific channel. RequestVote rejects stale history/term, disallowed membership or another known leader (transfer excepted), and persists vote before grant. Candidate majority enters Leader; newer term responses, received append, lease quorum loss or committed local removal exit it. Leadership transfer first catches the target up, suppresses new leader work, then sends TimeoutNow to trigger election without pre-vote. VerifyLeader separately registers an authority observation with replication workers and returns from aggregate support; that support eligibility is an open local question.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-recover\",\n        \"B-vote\",\n        \"B-election\",\n        \"B-leader-session\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-verify-register\",\n        \"B-verify-support\",\n        \"B-verify-consume\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-vote\",\n        \"F-authority\",\n        \"F-verify-support\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-api-verify\",\n        \"S-bootstrap\",\n        \"S-commitment\",\n        \"S-config-dispatch\",\n        \"S-config-replay\",\n        \"S-election\",\n        \"S-follower\",\n        \"S-fsm-worker\",\n        \"S-heartbeat\",\n        \"S-install\",\n        \"S-leader-loop\",\n        \"S-leader-session\",\n        \"S-lease\",\n        \"S-membership-change\",\n        \"S-membership-contract\",\n        \"S-notify\",\n        \"S-prevote-handler\",\n        \"S-prevote-producer\",\n        \"S-repl-membership\",\n        \"S-reply-match\",\n        \"S-send-snapshot\",\n        \"S-startup\",\n        \"S-term-persist\",\n        \"S-timeout-now\",\n        \"S-transfer\",\n        \"S-verify-register\",\n        \"S-verify-vote\",\n        \"S-vote-handler\",\n        \"S-vote-producer\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Every tenure creates a new commitment object, isolated replication workers and an initial term no-op. Existing durable history survives role loss, but old worker replies retain the old commitment/channel and do not certify a new tenure. Current-term commitment reconciles inherited history before allowing a new membership change. Membership activates latest voter eligibility at configuration append; retained voter matches survive by permanent ServerID, while new voters start at zero. Only one uncommitted configuration is admitted and committed local removal ends leadership. Exit fails pending inflight/verify futures, while already committed work queued to the FSM continues; ErrLeadershipLost is explicitly ambiguous about actual commitment. Recovery restores snapshot index/term/configuration and reconstructs latest configuration from retained logs. Snapshot production pairs applied state with committed configuration; manual Restore is an explicitly exceptional recovery operation that aborts inflight work and forces snapshot propagation followed by no-op commitment. Verification support differs from log support: all replication workers can notify pending verification, although voter filtering protects log commitment and lease quorum. This distinction supplies a focused question rather than a conclusion about safety.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-leader-session\",\n        \"B-commit\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-apply\",\n        \"B-recover\",\n        \"B-snapshot\",\n        \"B-user-restore\",\n        \"B-verify-support\",\n        \"B-verify-consume\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-peer-match\",\n        \"F-commit\",\n        \"F-authority\",\n        \"F-verify-support\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-api-apply\",\n        \"S-api-verify\",\n        \"S-append\",\n        \"S-bootstrap\",\n        \"S-commitment\",\n        \"S-config-dispatch\",\n        \"S-config-replay\",\n        \"S-dispatch-apply\",\n        \"S-election\",\n        \"S-fsm-contract\",\n        \"S-fsm-worker\",\n        \"S-heartbeat\",\n        \"S-install\",\n        \"S-leader-loop\",\n        \"S-leader-session\",\n        \"S-lease\",\n        \"S-membership-change\",\n        \"S-membership-contract\",\n        \"S-notify\",\n        \"S-repl-membership\",\n        \"S-reply-match\",\n        \"S-restore-api\",\n        \"S-restore-user\",\n        \"S-send-snapshot\",\n        \"S-snapshot-produce\",\n        \"S-startup\",\n        \"S-timeout-now\",\n        \"S-transfer\",\n        \"S-verify-register\",\n        \"S-verify-vote\",\n        \"S-vote-producer\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"VerifyLeader supporter eligibility, response timing and behavior across configuration activation\",\n      \"Heartbeat response term/contact asymmetry with blocked ordinary progress\",\n      \"Partial StableStore failure and network fast-path concurrency\",\n      \"Production store/snapshot failure variants, transport pipeline internals and manual RecoverCluster\",\n      \"Legacy interoperability and application-specific FSM behavior\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Representative normal command formation and authority acquisition/loss have been followed through real producers, consumers, membership, storage, recovery and completion. Usable identifies a sourced investigation basis, not verified correctness or exhaustive coverage.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"bb6faeab1df24b6f923838043e8fd549\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"bb6faeab1df24b6f923838043e8fd549\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e882dd28e3a74f959e62c629f3382252\",\n      \"question\": {\n        \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n        \"disposition\": \"concrete_suspicion\",\n        \"preferred_check\": \"controlled_schedule\",\n        \"requests\": [],\n        \"question\": \"Can VerifyLeader complete successfully using nonvoter worker support after this peer has lost effective leadership to a newer elected voter leader, and do the lease and negative-response paths prevent that outcome in a permitted execution?\",\n        \"importance\": \"VerifyLeader explicitly supports avoiding stale FSM reads after leadership loss. If nonvoters can supply sufficient verification support while the voter majority elects elsewhere, callers could treat an obsolete authority observation as permission to return stale data. This consequence requires an actual replacement-leader history and endpoint observation; code asymmetry alone does not establish it.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"S-api-verify\",\n          \"S-append\",\n          \"S-commitment\",\n          \"S-config-dispatch\",\n          \"S-config-replay\",\n          \"S-election\",\n          \"S-follower\",\n          \"S-heartbeat\",\n          \"S-leader-loop\",\n          \"S-leader-session\",\n          \"S-lease\",\n          \"S-membership-change\",\n          \"S-membership-contract\",\n          \"S-net-fastpath\",\n          \"S-notify\",\n          \"S-prevote-handler\",\n          \"S-prevote-producer\",\n          \"S-repl-membership\",\n          \"S-reply-match\",\n          \"S-send-snapshot\",\n          \"S-startup\",\n          \"S-timeout-now\",\n          \"S-transfer\",\n          \"S-verify-register\",\n          \"S-verify-vote\",\n          \"S-vote-producer\"\n        ],\n        \"participants\": [\n          \"Old leader\",\n          \"Remaining voter majority\",\n          \"Replicated nonvoter\",\n          \"VerifyLeader caller\"\n        ],\n        \"objects\": [\n          \"verifyFuture\",\n          \"followerReplication.notify\",\n          \"Latest configuration\",\n          \"Actual elected leader context\"\n        ],\n        \"contexts\": [\n          \"Stable protocol-v3 configuration containing voters and a nonvoter\",\n          \"One pending verification in an old leader tenure\",\n          \"Permitted transport partition/delay and real election in the voter component\"\n        ],\n        \"event_paths\": [\n          \"VerifyLeader -> verifyCh -> verifyLeader registration on every worker\",\n          \"Successful nonvoter reply -> notifyAll(true) -> vote(true) -> threshold -> leaderLoop future completion\",\n          \"Voter majority election competes with old leader lease expiry, negative reply and leader-session cleanup\"\n        ],\n        \"activity_classes\": [\n          \"A2\"\n        ],\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B-verify-support\",\n          \"B-verify-consume\",\n          \"B-leader-session\"\n        ],\n        \"fact_ids\": [\n          \"F-verify-support\"\n        ],\n        \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n          \"B-verify-register\": \"Defines captured quorum and all-worker registration before support delivery\",\n          \"B-membership\": \"Defines actual voter/nonvoter eligibility and creates replication workers for both\",\n          \"B-election\": \"Must establish newer authority through real vote production and consumption\",\n          \"B-append\": \"Actual receiver produces successful heartbeat responses with term checks\"\n        },\n        \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"Lease checks count voters only and can demote isolated leader.\",\n          \"Negative worker observation can fail pending verification and trigger step-down.\",\n          \"Old-session cleanup fails registered futures; stale higher-term ordinary append or snapshot responses signal step-down.\",\n          \"Log commitment independently filters nonvoters, so verification asymmetry does not itself show invalid log commitment.\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Applicable requirement: public VerifyLeader leadership guarantee is explicit, but voter-only verification must